<title>TAIWAN: Fujian approves Taiwan firms' China links -radio.</title>
<headline>Fujian approves Taiwan firms' China links -radio.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's Fujian province has given preliminary approval to at least four Taiwan shipping firms seeking permits to sail direct routes between Taiwan and rival China, Taiwan state radio said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The broadcast, which did not name its sources, said the applications to sail between Taiwan and Fujian's port at Xiamen had been forwarded to China's central government for review.</p>
<p>The broadcast identified the four firms as Yangming Marine Transport Corp, Uniglory Marine, Wan Hai Lines and Chinese Maritime Transport Ltd but said others also may have been approved.</p>
</text>
